# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Braining — .gitignore
#
# **`build/` and not `/build`.** A leading slash anchors the pattern to the repo
# root, so `/build` ignored one directory and left `app/build` (257 MB on
# 2026-08-30), `core-data/build`, and eight more perfectly visible to git. Caught
# before the first commit; a repository that starts by swallowing a quarter of a
# gigabyte of generated output never recovers its usefulness.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Build output — every module, not just the root.
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
/captures
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
/app/release/

# IDE
*.iml
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Machine-specific. `local.properties` holds the SDK path of whoever built last.
local.properties

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — the two lines that matter most in this file.
#
# `*.jks` is the signing key: losing control of it lets someone else publish an
# update to an app your friends have installed. `keystore.properties*` carries its
# password, and the `*` is deliberate — a `.bak` or `.cfg` copy holds exactly the
# same secret the original does, and a backup is precisely what gets committed by
# accident.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties*

# Build logs written by hand for diagnosis.
build-log*.txt

# Scratch produced by a review pass. Not part of the project.
.m5*-*.diff
